# debug.config — DISCOVERY-ONLY, NON-CONFORMING for validation
#
# Profile:        debug (crash analysis / root-cause analysis)
# Kbase:          r54p0-01eac0 (primary)  [+ patches/virtual-device/ 0001-0006]
# Kernel:         6.12.111 — the pinned, VERIFIED-working kernel
#                 (kernel/sources/kernel.pin; baseline built on it, F-18).
#                 NOTE: the newest LTS 6.18.54 does NOT build (F-16), so "latest
#                 LTS" is not available for this project.
# Patch set:      vendor/virtual-device/ 0001-0006 + kernel/patches/0001-* (F-17)
# Scope class:    DISCOVERY-ONLY / NON-CONFORMING FOR VALIDATION
#                 CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL and the DWARF choice are NOT on the Arm
#                 kernel allowlist (program-scope.md §5), and CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG=y
#                 violates the MANDATORY MALI_DEBUG=n (program-scope.md §8.3).
#                 Usable to DIAGNOSE; never a conforming validation environment.
# Generated from: Arm's virtual-platform guide Kbase options + generic debug
#                 symbols. Every Kbase symbol below has since been VERIFIED
#                 against r54p0's own Kconfig and against the pinned tree; the
#                 Linux debug symbols were named from mainline knowledge and two
#                 of them (DEBUG_INFO, MALI_KUTF) were WRONG on first write --
#                 F-24 and F-27. check/check-all.sh A2 now gates every line in
#                 this file against the real Kconfig, so a repeat cannot land.
# Validation:     BUILT + BOOTED 2026-10-01 on 6.12.111. 16/16 fragment symbols
#                 took effect (build/logs/debug.log step 5); `mali_kbase.ko` 53 MB
#                 and `bzImage` 13.6 MB produced; the EL0 probe passed 0x1ff with
#                 0x000 failed. DWARF5 debug info is confirmed in the IMAGE, not
#                 just the config: vmlinux carries .debug_info/.debug_line_str/
#                 .debug_rnglists/.debug_loclists and readelf reports
#                 `Version: 5`. Log: research/boot-logs/20261001T111658Z-debug-BOOT.log
# Config hash:    merged .config 67405d143d94c32524ca1c352dae75c527cb9f71d58e26036d2216bc182a3610
#                 (build/logs/debug.log step 5)
# Bundle:        artifacts/debug, TARGET_VERIFIED. NOT yet PORTABLE_ARTIFACT_VERIFIED
#                 (no clean-location boot yet).
#
# NOT a valid .config. NOT the output of make defconfig/savedefconfig. It is a
# FRAGMENT merged onto x86_64_defconfig by kernel/scripts/build.sh.

# Purpose: crash analysis and root-cause. This is a diagnosis profile, not a
# throughput profile, and not a validation environment (see Scope class; project
# spec §16, §24 / F-9).

# --- Linux debug (NOT on the Arm allowlist — discovery only) --------------
# Do NOT assume generic DEBUG_KERNEL / DEBUG_INFO / LOCKDEP / DEBUG_VM are
# allowed; none of them are on the allowlist. Anything added here beyond
# CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL / the DWARF choice must be individually classified as
# NON-CONFORMING before use.
CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
# F-24: this was `CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO=y`, which is UNSATISFIABLE and silently
# discarded. `DEBUG_INFO` exists at lib/Kconfig.debug:227 but is a prompt-less
# derived `bool`, `select`ed by the members of the "Debug information" choice
# (DEBUG_INFO_NONE / _DWARF_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULT / _DWARF4 / _DWARF5). A symbol
# with no prompt can never be set from a config fragment, so the line did
# nothing and the build's step-5 gate stopped the build (correctly).
#
# DWARF5 is chosen over DEBUG_INFO_DWARF_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULT deliberately: the
# "toolchain default" would make the debug-info format of the packaged artifact
# depend on the host gcc version, and this repository's product is meant to be
# reproducible. Pinning the version keeps the bundle self-describing.
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_DWARF5=y

# --- Kbase driver options -------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD=m
CONFIG_MALI_CSF_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_MALI_EXPERT=y
CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI=y
# CONFIG_MALI_REAL_HW is not set
# Latest GPU target defined by r54p0 (DECISION-2); investigation-only.
CONFIG_MALI_NO_MALI_DEFAULT_GPU="tDRx"
CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_NAME="vexpress"

# --- Kbase debug: DISCOVERY-ONLY (violates mandatory MALI_DEBUG=n) ---------
# Program policy REQUIRES CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG=n and permits only the five §8.3
# options to change (research/program-scope.md §8.3). This profile deliberately
# violates that to get Kbase's own debug paths, so it is NON-CONFORMING and may
# be used for investigation only — never as a validation environment.
CONFIG_MALI_DEBUG=y

# F-27: MALI_DEBUG=y has a build-breaking side effect that is not obvious from
# the Kconfig name. `midgard/tests/Kconfig:21` reads
#     menuconfig MALI_KUTF  depends on MALI_MIDGARD && MALI_DEBUG
#                          default y if MALI_DEBUG
# so opting into Kbase debug paths SILENTLY opts this profile into building
# Kbase's unit-test framework (kutf.ko, kutf_test.ko). That code does not compile
# on x86_64/6.12: tests/kutf/kutf_kprobe.c:139 uses `ri->rph`, guarded only by
# LINUX_VERSION_CODE, but include/linux/kprobes.h:162 defines `rph` only when
# CONFIG_KRETPROBE_ON_RETHOOK is off — and arch/Kconfig:208 sets it `def_bool y`.
# This is a config-dependent API break, not a version break.
#
# The kutf modules are Kbase's self-tests and are not needed for crash analysis;
# they are excluded rather than patched. Stated limitation: this profile does NOT
# build Kbase's unit tests. Re-enabling them requires a kutf_kprobe.c patch that
# tests CONFIG_KRETPROBE_ON_RETHOOK instead of the version.
# CONFIG_MALI_KUTF is not set

# --- Kernel hard build gates, set explicitly ------------------------------
# VERIFIED: midgard/Kbuild raises $(error ...) for FIVE unconditional symbols at
# lines 29,33,37,41,45. The test is `ifeq ($(CONFIG_X),n)`, which does NOT catch
# an unset symbol. DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND was MISSING from an earlier
# revision of these fragments; see findings.md F-3 and F-11.
# F-26 INERT: this line cannot take effect. DMA_SHARED_BUFFER is a prompt-less
# `bool` (drivers/base/Kconfig:200) and is therefore unreachable from a config
# fragment. It IS y in the built .config because Kbase's own Kconfig selects it
# (midgard/Kconfig:23) -- not because of this line. The gate is genuinely met;
# the line is kept only as the record of the requirement. Do not read its
# presence as evidence that this profile controls the symbol.
CONFIG_DMA_SHARED_BUFFER=y
CONFIG_PM_DEVFREQ=y
CONFIG_DEVFREQ_THERMAL=y
CONFIG_DEVFREQ_GOV_SIMPLE_ONDEMAND=y
CONFIG_FW_LOADER=y

# --- Resolved during the build phase (was: UNRESOLVED) ---------------------
# - Exact kernel version: RESOLVED -> 6.12.111 (kernel/sources/kernel.pin).
#   The newest LTS (6.18.54) does not build r54p0 (F-16), so "latest LTS" is
#   unavailable for this driver; the pin stays 6.12.111.
# - MALI_NO_MALI is on here too, for the virtual harness (RESOLVED, DECISION-1).
# - CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO: UNSATISFIABLE (F-24) -> replaced by the DWARF5 choice.
# - CONFIG_MALI_KUTF: MUST be off (F-27) -> the unit-test framework does not
#   compile on x86_64/6.12 under KRETPROBE_ON_RETHOOK.
# - Additional debug options are still gated: anything beyond the two lines above
#   must be individually classified NON-CONFORMING before use (§5 / §8.3).
